Source data
-----------

Each table declares its provenance: `sources` (organisation, title, year,
URL) and a `referenceYear`, or `assumption: true` with a `justification`.
The figures are aggregates and facts taken from public statistics, cited
rather than copied from any publication. The original data remain under the
terms of their publishers, which require citing the source, for example:

  - France: INSEE and other public bodies, under the Licence Ouverte /
    Open Licence of Etalab (https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/)
  - Singapore: SingStat (Department of Statistics), MOM, CPF Board, IRAS,
    HDB and others, under the Singapore Open Data Licence
    (https://data.gov.sg/open-data-licence) or the terms of each publisher

When you reuse a table, keep its `sources` block.
